Bugs/Issues

    - MEMORY RUNAWAY: Each call to the agama_initfromfile() routine creates a new pointer object, increasing the memory by ~50 MB. Since the AGAMA Fortran interface does not provide a destructor, repeated calls to the routine eventually lead to the memory being exhausted.
    A workaround at the moment is to limit the calls via a t_step variable.


